From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 00:57:32 -0500
Subject: feat: spaces that share a named session (S-272)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Several Spaces can now be on one session, as several Arc Spaces are on one
profile (GitHub issues 8 and 99; ADR 0034). The two commits before this one made
a session an id and a name, and a jar something wiped only when no Space names
it; this one gives the user the choice and carries it everywhere a Space goes.

Edit Space has a Session row under the name, and Settings' Space row has the same
choice where its switch was: Shared, a session already there, or "New session…".
Edit Space shows a field for the new name under the choice and Done applies it.
Settings asks for the name in a small window. One switch could not say which
session (sessions S39). A change goes through the question turning a session on
or off asks, with the same count of pages and the same line for apps, and moves
the tabs by the same road, so a page with unsaved changes keeps its jar until it
is left. There is no Undo, as there is none for S10 (S40).

The questions tell the truth about a jar several Spaces name. Deleting a Space
says the session stays and who keeps it, or that it is erased, for a Space whose
session is off too. Clear Independent Session names every Space that shares it
(S41, S46). Settings lists a session no Space uses, with Delete Session… (S45).
The mark names the session and the others while it is shared, its title row says
the essentials are the session's, and site controls name the session (S48). An
app is named only when no other Space then uses its session (S52). What an
essential of a session opens stays in the Space on screen (S47).

Export writes a Space's session when it has a name of its own, and sync carries
it in one field, id and name together, so they merge as one. A Space's lone
session stays the flag it was, so a file and a peer from before this mean what
they meant (S50, S51). Import and sync go by the id and never by the name: a
Space they make takes the session with that id, new and empty when this install
has none, and an existing Space never moves on its own (sidebar-file Sf24, Join
here or Not on this computer). An id that is not a token is left out.

Arc's Spaces that shared a custom profile in one import now share one new
session named after it, on an empty jar; a Space on Arc's default profile stays
Shared, and nothing joins a session already here (import I8). That part was
checked with a made-up file shaped like the importer's existing fixture.

Why: GitHub issues 8 and 99, and r/Stedding: several Spaces signed in as one
account and others as another, the arrangement a person leaving Arc already has.

Removable when: never; this is the feature.
